Heeler: let one node use independent root sets (the planet plus local moons).

Heeler joins each ZeroTier network through its own roots: ZeroTier's planet
for networks on ZeroTier's controllers, and a self-hosted planet for a
network that names one, which the app turns into a locally built moon.
ZeroTier 1.x assumes all of a node's upstreams share one peer database: it
sends every WHOIS, relayed packet, and multicast GATHER to the single
lowest-latency upstream, which drops what it cannot deliver. With
independent root sets the nearer set hides the other's peers (measured: a
self-hosted root at 35 ms made an official network's controller
unreachable). Knowing a peer's identity is no sign of reaching it, either:
ZeroTier's roots answer WHOIS for nodes that once used them, so a WHOIS
answer cannot pick the relay.

This patch:
- sends WHOIS to the best upstream of each root set (the planet's roots,
  and each moon's), Switch::requestWhois;
- remembers, per peer, the upstream that relayed that peer's packets to
  this node, for ZT_HEELER_LEARNED_VIA_TTL (two minutes) since last seen
  and while the peer is known (Topology::noteRelayedVia, doPeriodicTasks);
- relays through that upstream, or else through the best upstream of each
  root set, of the destination's own set when it is a root
  (Topology::getRelaysFor in Switch::_trySend), and GATHERs multicast the
  same way for the network's controller (Multicaster);
- adds Node::addLocalMoon, which takes a serialized moon built by the
  caller (heeler_zt_add_moon); Node::deorbit removes it.

With only ZeroTier's planet there is one root set, so lookups, relaying,
and GATHER go to the single best upstream as before. Each changed file
carries a "Modified by Heeler contributors" notice.

Applies to libzt commit a707ea6ae0910efdc1125d04758c411e2e9ea4f9 with its
ext/ZeroTierOne submodule at c53c6bd9c320ea839c525972d8afba448a58606e.

